Subject: [PATCH] Add pluggable PostgreSQL backend for large-scale deployments

- Split db/database.py into db/backends/{sqlite_backend,postgres_backend}.py
- db/database.py is now a thin facade that picks the backend from
  config.yaml (database.type: sqlite | postgres), so no call sites in
  tracking/, analytics/, or api/ need to change
- New PostgreSQL backend uses a threaded connection pool (psycopg2) so
  it stays correct under concurrent camera-ingestion threads + API reads
- Add db/schema_postgres.sql (structural mirror of schema.sql)
- Add scripts/migrate_sqlite_to_postgres.py to carry over existing data
- Document the switch in README.md, add psycopg2-binary to requirements
